sformers (doc `utility-capex-2027`).\n- **Debt is open but costlier:** Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 2026 to 165bp. Norvane still priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably (doc `utility-credit`).\n- **Equity is the weak point:** Two utility share offerings were cut back (doc `utility-credit`). Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after demand fell short. It is cutting 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and deferring two substation programmes \"until financing improves\" (doc `pellham-offering`).\n\n**Reading:**\n- **Norvane** looks able to fund its plan through bonds, at wider spreads.\n- **Pellham** apparently can't fund its plan with debt alone. The C$2.4B equity raise was part of its financing, and it has chosen to cut capex rather than replace that equity with debt. The documents don't say why. It could be a leverage or rating limit, or a preference to protect its credit.\n- **Knock-on effect:** Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria. Its 40% cut in transformer orders will hit suppliers.\n\n**Gaps:** I found no data on either company's leverage, rating headroom, total funding need, or the size of future debt issuance. A firmer answer needs those figures.","ttft_ms":2494,"type":"result","duration_ms":20007,"uuid":"e7eb3e88-9da9-4511-a401-110bf984ca1a","ttft_stream_ms":1418,"time_to_request_ms":71,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":14,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":10,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":7,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":4},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":21,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":70,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_t